{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#1369","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#1369","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#1369\",\"parent_revision\":\"d3209b062ad7fb0d638b1d77703c22f1139f9b98\",\"root_revision\":\"a4ff68965191048cab52b8c863480c3a8c8eb7ad2e5a7b393c62312f31c10818\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-12\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nWhen a session begins working on a backlog item (via work-backlog-item), it must register a claim record that is visible to any other session on any machine. The claim must survive process death \u2014 it cannot live only in local state.\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAssessment date: 2026-04-23\\n\\n| # | Condition | Status | Source |\\n|---|-----------|--------|--------|\\n| 1 | GitHub issue label or comment as claim storage mechanism | AVAILABLE | MCP backlog tools support label add/remove and comment |\\n| 2 | `work-backlog-item` skill entry points for claim registration | AVAILABLE | `plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/` |\\n| 3 | Session ID accessible in Claude Code sessions | DERIVABLE | Check `CLAUDE_SESSION_ID` or equivalent env var |\\n| 4 | Machine hostname accessible | AVAILABLE | `platform.node()` or `socket.gethostname()` |\\n| 5 | Claim label format (e.g., `claimed:session-abc123`) | MISSING | Must be designed |\\n| 6 | Stale claim detection threshold | MISSING | 24h proposed in item but not decided |\\n\\nVerdict: READY with minor design decisions \u2014 label format and TTL can be decided during implementation.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **session-aware work claim system for backlog items** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Transcript analysis \u2014 concurrent --auto sessions, crash/kill/credit-exhaustion scenarios\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-04-01\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-04-23)\\n\\n### Impact\\n\\nP1 Feature. Affects work-backlog-item skill and backlog MCP server. Requires new GitHub labels. Medium complexity.\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n- When `work-backlog-item` begins working on an item, it registers a claim in GitHub issue metadata (label or comment) that is machine-readable\\n- The claim record includes: session ID, machine hostname, start timestamp, item number\\n- Any other session calling `work-backlog-item` on the same item detects the active claim and either blocks or warns\\n- Claim is automatically released when the session completes or the item reaches a terminal state (groomed, done, closed)\\n- Claim survives process death \u2014 it lives on GitHub, not in local state\\n- CLI/MCP tool to manually release a stale claim (for cases where the session died without releasing)\\n- Claim TTL: claims older than 24 hours are treated as stale and auto-released on next access\\n\\n### Files\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/` \u2014 add claim registration/release\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py` \u2014 add `backlog_claim` and `backlog_release` tools\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/github.py` \u2014 claim label management\\n\\n### Story\\n\\nAs a backlog session starting work on an item, I need to register a durable claim record visible to any other session on any machine so that two sessions never work on the same item simultaneously and claim state survives process death.\\n\\n## Out Of Scope\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- Distributed locking with true atomicity guarantees (GitHub Issues are not a mutex)\\n- UI dashboard (separate issue)\\n- Automatic stale reclaim (human decision required)\\n</div>\\n\\n## Requirements\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n**Claim record fields (all required):**\\n- `claimed_at` \u2014 ISO 8601 timestamp when work started\\n- `machine` \u2014 hostname of the machine that claimed it\\n- `session_id` \u2014 Claude Code session ID (from CLAUDE_SESSION_ID env or equivalent)\\n- `branch` \u2014 git branch at time of claim\\n- `pid` \u2014 process ID (for local liveness check when on same machine)\\n\\n**Persistence:**\\n- Stored in the GitHub Issue body as a structured section (source of truth, cross-machine)\\n- Local cache in `~/.dh/projects/{slug}/backlog/{item}.md` kept in sync by MCP server\\n\\n**Queryability:**\\n- `backlog_list` should expose claim metadata (claimed_at, machine, session_id, branch) per item\\n- New MCP tool `backlog_list_claims` (or filter on `backlog_list`) \u2014 return all in-progress items with full claim records, sortable by age\\n- Stale threshold configurable (default: no heartbeat for >1h = stale candidate)\\n\\n**Stale detection:**\\n- Claim is \\\"active\\\" if claimed_at is recent OR a heartbeat has been written\\n- Claim is \\\"stale\\\" if no heartbeat for >N minutes (configurable, default 60)\\n- Claim is \\\"orphaned\\\" if pid is dead (only detectable on same machine)\\n- `work-backlog-item` must check for an existing claim before setting its own \u2014 if claim exists and is not stale, report it and stop (do not silently overwrite)\\n\\n**Heartbeat:**\\n- Session writes a heartbeat timestamp to the claim record periodically while active\\n- Heartbeat stored in same GitHub Issue section (or as a structured comment to avoid body churn)\\n\\n**Release:**\\n- Claim is released when `resolve` or `close` is called\\n- Claim can be force-released with `backlog_release_claim {item}` (for orphaned/stale cleanup)\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"9b0400690521ed1cf038b551029d549bca4323ad7325821d3a19e935e3431331\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPtaUAA\"}"}